<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Diaspora.Modules.Marketplace</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Diaspora.Modules.Marketplace</AssemblyName>
    <Description>
      The Marketplace &amp; Commerce Platform (Phase B10). The platform's single owner of trade
      between members: what is for sale, who is selling it, what was offered for it, who reserved
      it, and whether it sold.

      A listing is not a classified advert. It belongs to a seller profile that may be a person or
      a business, carries a price in a stated currency that nothing silently converts, tracks its
      own stock, moves through a lifecycle from draft to sold, and stops being discoverable the
      moment it is reserved out. An offer is not a message: it is a durable negotiation with an
      append-only history, an expiry, and exactly one accepted terminal state. A reservation is not
      a flag: it holds stock against a named buyer until it completes, expires or is cancelled, and
      returns the stock in every one of those cases.

      What Marketplace owns: listings, seller profiles, offers, reservations, saved listings,
      reports, promotions, conversation references, the listing analytics rollup and the commerce
      catalogues. What it deliberately does not: the badge on a seller belongs to Trust, the
      country a listing sits in belongs to Location, the photograph bytes belong to Media, the shop
      behind a storefront belongs to Providers, the discussion under a listing belongs to
      Community, and the chat between buyer and seller will belong to the Communication module.
      Marketplace reaches every one of them through published contracts and stores identifiers,
      never copies.

      Search is a seam, not an engine: the module ships an EF-backed search over the write model
      and the IMarketplaceSearchEngine port an OpenSearch adapter can satisfy later without a
      domain change. Ranking, categories, category attributes, fraud signals, view de-duplication
      and buyer/seller conversations are contributor seams on the same terms.

      Payments, cart, checkout, escrow, shipment tracking, warehouse management, the auction engine
      and dynamic pricing are explicitly out of scope, and the abstractions here are shaped so that
      each arrives as a new module rather than as a restructuring of this one.

      Registers entirely through B2.6 contributor interfaces: no edit to the Platform Kernel, the
      Identity module, Trust, Location, Media, Community, Providers, Guides, Jobs, or Program.cs.
    </Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    B9's reference set. Location, Media, Community, Providers and Guides are deliberate and
    documented. B10 consumes Location's published Integration and Extensibility contracts
    (IGeographicScopeResolver, INearbyResourceProvider, ILocationResourceCounter), Media's
    published reference contracts (attach-by-reference, never URLs — and
    MediaOwnerType.MarketplaceListing has existed since B5), Community's published Extensibility
    contract (ICommunityContentSource — and CommunityContentType.Marketplace has existed since
    B6), Providers' published IProviderDirectory for the shops behind a storefront, and Guides'
    published IGuideDirectory for the buying-safely explainers beside a listing.

    Notably absent: the Identity module, the Trust module and the Jobs module. Marketplace reaches
    Identity through the kernel's ICurrentUser and Trust through Diaspora.Contracts — the published
    ITrustVerificationSubmission contract and Trust's published integration events — never through
    their aggregates. Jobs is not consumed at all: the two verticals are siblings, and a reference
    between them would be the first edge in the graph B2.6 exists to keep acyclic. Architecture
    tests enforce all four.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MediatR" />
    <PackageReference Include="FluentValidation" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options.ConfigurationExtensions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.SharedKernel\Diaspora.SharedKernel.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Contracts\Diaspora.Contracts.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Platform\Diaspora.Platform.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Application\Diaspora.Application.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Persistence\Diaspora.Persistence.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Location\Diaspora.Modules.Location.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Media\Diaspora.Modules.Media.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Community\Diaspora.Modules.Community.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Providers\Diaspora.Modules.Providers.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Guides\Diaspora.Modules.Guides.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
